        "start": 3
      },
      "schema_version": "1.0.0",
      "status": "supported",
      "text": "JUSTICE SCALIA: You haven't changed your mind in the interim, have you?"
    },
    {
      "attribution": "Petitioner (Kuntrell Jackson)",
      "case_id": "2011-10-9647",
      "confidence": 1.0,
      "document_hash": "1d17a9f8eeea4bffeaf349d9d4ba207d75a06b4a5de88baa118f1ebcad6c5099",
      "evidence_id": "ev-1d17a9f8eeea-0000-0003",
      "kind": "party_argument",
      "opinion_part": null,
      "pages": {
        "end": 4,
        "start": 4
      },
      "schema_version": "1.0.0",
      "status": "supported",
      "text": "MR. STEVENSON: Well, I -- I think you -- you could do that. In fact, in Graham, the Court makes these statements that they're trying to exempt and shield juveniles who did not kill, quote, \"or did not intend to kill.\" And that language could be a basis for organizing the Court's thinking on this issue."
    },
    {
      "attribution": "Petitioner (Kuntrell Jackson)",
      "case_id": "2011-10-9647",
      "confidence": 1.0,
      "document_hash": "1d17a9f8eeea4bffeaf349d9d4ba207d75a06b4a5de88baa118f1ebcad6c5099",
